Ukraine’s defence-tech sector is growing quickly. This expansion, combined with major public contracts and complex supply chains, has increased law enforcement scrutiny.

Recent searches of Ukrainian defence companies demonstrate that even compliant businesses can face major disruptions if unprepared. Seized devices, inaccessible documents, blocked accounts, and uncoordinated employee responses can quickly lead to operational and reputational risks.

In a new article for Defender Media, Anastasiia Didenko, Counsel and Head of WCC, Anti-Corruption & Compliance at LCF Law Group, outlines how defence companies can prepare in advance for investigations, including:

▪️ Establishing a clear internal response protocol;
▪️ Training employees and appointing designated contacts;
▪️ Reviewing contracts, transactions and counterparties;
▪️ Protecting corporate data and electronic devices;
▪️ Checking the legal basis and scope of a search;
▪️ Documenting procedural violations.

The article concludes with a practical checklist to help businesses assess if their internal procedures are ready for searches or other investigative actions.

